{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 52, :comments ["<b>This heap and this pillar.</b> After saying ״Elohim is witness between me and you,״ why did he need to go back and say ״this heap״? But he did so in order to call heaven and earth as witnesses through this. And so Samuel the prophet said to Israel (I Samuel 12:5): ״HaShem is witness against you, and His anointed is witness.״" "<b>If I do not pass over to you.</b> That is, 'I.' And this crossing over is for evil, as the end of the verse proves, for thus we find the language of crossing over in the context of war (Leviticus 26:6): ״and the sword shall not pass through your land.״ And the covenant they both made is that neither would cross the other's border, for the Gilead is the border of the land of Israel, as it is written (Deuteronomy 34:1): ״and HaShem showed him all the land, the Gilead unto Dan,״ and this is what it says לרעה — for evil, that is, in order to harm one another. And so our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: לרעה — you may not cross, but you may cross for commerce. And Balaam the wicked, who was of the seed of Laban and from Pethor of Aram Naharaim, his city, began to violate this covenant — this is what is written (Deuteronomy 23:5): ״but because they hired against you Balaam son of Beor,״ etc. And after him, Cushan-Rishathaim — this is what is written (Judges 3:8): ״and the anger of HaShem was kindled against Israel,״ etc. And on this account David was permitted to wage war against him when he campaigned against Aram Naharaim, and it is written (II Samuel 8:6): ״and David placed garrisons in Aram.״" "<b>And know</b> that Aram Naharaim is Damascus, and it is called Aram Naharaim on account of the two rivers that are in it, as it is said (II Kings 5:12): ״Are not Amanah and Pharpar, the rivers of Damascus, better,״ and concerning it Elijah was told, (I Kings 19:15): ״Go, return on your way to the wilderness of Damascus, and anoint Hazael to be king over Aram.״"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:57.034792995Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}